    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### AI substrate \u2014 occupancy is not work\n`DCGM_FI_DEV_GPU_UTIL` reports only that **a kernel was resident**. A card pinned at 100% can be nearly idle; a card at 0% can be holding gigabytes of weights that must not be evicted. Every panel here is arranged so that number can be checked against something real.\n\n**On this card the profiling fields are unavailable.** `DCGM_FI_PROF_*` (SM_ACTIVE, DRAM_ACTIVE) are Data Center Profiling fields and the module does not load on GeForce \u2014 a product boundary, not a misconfiguration. So work is inferred from three angles instead: **memory-controller utilization** as a bandwidth proxy, **clocks** as evidence of throttling, and **violation counters** for how long a tenant was actually being capped. Coarser than SM_ACTIVE. Still enough to catch every lie util tells."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "GPU util (naive)",
      "description": "Kernel residency. The control series \u2014 never the verdict.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
